── UNKNOWN NAME ──────────────────────── E0211_java_string_type.lt:1:16  [E0211]

Stilt's string type is `str`, not `String`:

  1 │ fn greet(name: String) -> str { "hello, {name}" }
    │                ^^^^^^

Stilt's primitive types are written in lower case, as `i64`, `f64`, `bool` and
`str`.

To fix it, write `str`:

  1 │ fn greet(name: str) -> str { "hello, {name}" }
    │                ~~~
